# Copy this file to .env.local for local dev (vercel dev), and set the same
# vars in the Vercel dashboard (Project -> Settings -> Environment Variables)
# for Production/Preview. Never commit real values — .env.local is gitignored.

# Required. Get one at https://openrouter.ai/settings/keys — set a credit
# limit on the key itself in that dashboard as a hard spend cap.
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# Optional. Defaults to openai/gpt-4o-mini if unset. Any OpenRouter model slug
# works — see https://openrouter.ai/models for current options/pricing.
OPENROUTER_MODEL=

# Optional. Logs every Ovid exchange (timestamp, conversation id, turn
# number, type, the user's message, and Ovid's reply) as a row in a Google
# Sheet, so you can review real conversations and tweak the knowledge base.
# Leave unset to disable logging entirely — nothing breaks either way.
#
# Setup:
#   1. Create a new Google Sheet. In row 1, add these headers:
#      Timestamp | Conversation ID | Turn | Type | User Message | Reply
#   2. Extensions -> Apps Script. Delete the placeholder code and paste in
#      the script from docs/ovid-log-apps-script.js in this repo.
#   3. Deploy -> New deployment -> type "Web app". Execute as "Me", who has
#      access: "Anyone". Deploy, authorize it, and copy the Web App URL.
#   4. Paste that URL below (and in Vercel's dashboard for Production).
OVID_LOG_WEBHOOK_URL=
